eria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5246,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["materialize-mcp-upstream.sh installs the seed 'ONLY IF absent' and defers to a flip that 'may own it' (mcp-upstream.conf:9-11)","mcp service uses `--restart always` (docker-compose.yml:324) and the plan reproduces `--restart always` for `mcp_run_new`","compose-up.sh:197 re-runs materialize-mcp-upstream.sh and re-brings-up compose-mcp-1 on 8091 at boot","plan states 'autodeploy never `docker compose up mcp`' and only resets the include to 8091 as a ROLLBACK step, not on a routine reboot"],"finding":"The plan does not specify how the post-reboot state reconciles: after a deploy the nginx include points at 8092/8093 and materialize-mcp-upstream.sh leaves it untouched on the next boot, while compose-up.sh brings compose-mcp-1 back on 8091. Depending on whether the last blue-green container (with --restart always) or the compose-original survived the reboot, /mcp's include may name a freed/dead port until the next deploy, and the managed-set/port accounting sees both compose-mcp-1 and a blue-green container simultaneously.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c8f42ec82aea159","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Run mechanism + managed set / Compat / rollback","norm_id":"n78d78c3a280bbed0","priority":0.0754,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Box reboots after an mcp deploy: include points at 8092, compose-mcp-1 comes up on 8091, the blue-green container on 8092 restarts (or was already rm'd, leaving 8092 with no backend)","Managed-set count on the first post-reboot tick sees both compose-mcp-1 and a blue-green container, affecting cap/sweep logic"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisf